      "id": 1,
      "text": "Willington was officially incorporated in May 1727, keeping the original spelling of its name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willington%2C_Connecticut",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Settlers first called the area Wellington in 1725, after the English town that was the birthplace of Roger Wolcott’s grandfather.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willington%2C_Connecticut",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Willimantic River borders Willington on the west, a feature that supported its early grazing and lumbering industries.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willington%2C_Connecticut",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Daniel Glazier Tavern opened in 1815, and its upstairs ballroom served as a town meetinghouse for almost thirty years.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willington%2C_Connecticut",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A new public library opened in autumn 2006, replacing the former Hall Memorial School location.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willington%2C_Connecticut",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
